// EXPECT: PASS
// A multi-word name must not care about the amount or kind of whitespace
// between its words - space, repeated spaces, a tab, or a newline should
// all normalize to the same name. Re-opening the same name with a
// different amount of whitespace each time is the strongest check
// run_tests.sh can make of this (it only checks the exit code): if the
// words were joined differently each time, the name wouldn't match and
// this would either fail to parse or (see cpp/ToDo) silently create a
// separate anonymous object instead of re-opening the same one - the
// former shows up here, the latter doesn't (run_tests.sh doesn't check
// tree contents), so this was also confirmed by hand with `-a`.
TOP {
	Family Name: {
		Original: Object;
	}
	Family   Name {			// Extra spaces
		ExtraSpaces: Object;
	}
	Family	Name {			// A tab
		TabSeparated: Object;
	}
	Family
		Name {			// A newline (plus leading whitespace)
		NewlineSeparated: Object;
	}
	One Two Three: Object;		// Three words, not just two
}
